# .gitattributes - line endings for every checkout, on every OS.
# WHY: Git for Windows converts LF to CRLF on checkout by default
# (core.autocrlf=true). A shell script with CRLF endings fails in sh
# ("$'\r': command not found"), so text files keep LF everywhere. Windows
# batch files are the exception: cmd.exe expects CRLF.
# Reference: https://git-scm.com/docs/gitattributes#_eol
* text=auto eol=lf
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf
